   - Only use LinkedList if you're doing lots of addFirst/removeLast

4. NEVER USE:
   - Vector (use ArrayList)
   - Hashtable (use HashMap)
   - Stack (use ArrayDeque)

5. REMEMBER:
   - Set.add() returns false if element already exists (useful for duplicates!)
   - Map.merge() is perfect for counting
   - Map.computeIfAbsent() is perfect for grouping
   - Streams make transformations clean (but learn loops first!)

6. LEETCODE TIP:
   - Two Sum → HashMap
   - Valid Parentheses → Stack
   - Top K Elements → PriorityQueue
   - Sliding Window Maximum → Deque
*/

